       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day under prescription labeling, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **800 mg orally four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum, usually for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg orally four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg orally every 4-6 hours as needed** for pain or fever, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n\nWas 1,600 mg meant to be the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily? Or was a different drug or dose intended? Tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If you need something above the labeled maximum, that should go through pharmacy or the attending physician."
